WEBVTT

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:33.200
I can't even fly anymore.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.370
But this is only temporary.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:40.000
Once my back heals up and I feel better

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.390
I'll teach you so many things.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:48.560
If I feel like it, I can move a mountain

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.770
or mow down buildings with a whirlwind.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.400
Yes, I'm sure you can.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.680
As I am now I'm just too pitiful.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:05.630
But I'll be terrorizing everything 
under the sun again soon...

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.610
Professor, please go to sleep.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.100
I'm going, I'm going.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.750
You should sleep here once in a while, too.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.330
This is so sad.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.990
1,200 years since Emperor Kammu settled 
on a location for the palace...

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.660
Humans live in the city, 
tanuki crawl the earth,

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.250
tengu fly through the air.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.050
Since the Heian era relocation, humans, tanuki, 
and tengu have maintained a delicate balance.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:52.420
That's what keeps the great wheel of 
this city turning round and round.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:57.820
More fun than anything is 
watching that wheel spin.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:06.630
I'm what you'd call a tanuki, but 
too proud to be a <i>mere</i> tanuki,

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:11.440
I admire tengu from afar 
and love imitating humans.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.840
For that reason, my daily 
life is so dizzyingly busy

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.930
there's no time to be bored.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.000
<b>Episode 2: Mom and Raijin, God of Thunder</b>

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.730
Here I am, back again.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:15.700
Welcome, Prince. Your companion 
today is a young lady?

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:19.920
If I would have known you were coming 
I would have had those guys wait.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.480
What guys?

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.000
A bunch of guys from a TV station.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.950
They wanted to do a story on the Prince in 
black everyone in town is talking about.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.610
Well it seems I can't live a quiet life.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:34.220
No matter where I go the rumors start flying.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:38.290
Oh? In that case, next time they come 
I'll tell them it's okay to film.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:47.340
So I heard from Yashiro that 
you were out yesterday--

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.670
Mother, you can talk normally.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.290
There's nobody here.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.100
Did you meet up with Benten again yesterday?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.620
Yeah, well.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.900
But that's so dangerous!

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.990
It's fine.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:05.510
She's crazy. If you're not careful 
you'll get boiled in a hot pot.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.680
Tanuki have been boiled in 
hot pots since ancient times, but...

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.540
Anyhow, humans are more treacherous 
and nasty than even tengu or kitsune.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.350
Prof. Akadama asked me 
to see her, so I had to.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:24.780
The professor should know better at his 
age than to get infatuated like that.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.510
People like him cause the most trouble.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.540
Oh, the prince is here.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.310
Yo, if it isn't Andy!

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.430
It's Ando. How about a rematch?

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.030
I was hoping you'd say that, Andy.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:40.610
I'm gonna go to Yajiro's.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:44.990
Oh? Well, please make sure he's still alive.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:50.090
You know you could just go see him, Mother. 
You haven't gone even once, right?

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:53.380
He would hate it if I went.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:57.200
He's over there doing what he 
does because he believes in it,

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.880
but I'm ashamed of it.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:03.970
The weather's bad today, 
so don't stay out too long.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:07.780
Yasaburo, on your way back swing 
by the Ebisugawa power plant

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.340
and pick up Yashiro.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.390
Prince, where do you want to play?

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.530
I'll come by you.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.720
I'm sorry!

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:49.110
Shimogamo Yashiro, how many 
times has it been now?

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:52.020
There's nothing left for me 
to take out of your wages.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.140
You're in debt now, sheer debt!

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.170
But, the one who bumped into me was--

00:06:56.170 --> 00:07:00.330
Are you trying to pin the blame 
on me? Big Brother, tell him off!

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.030
You're a terrible nuisance!

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.200
Huh?

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:07.090
It's enlightened vocabulary 
used to abuse those

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:10.800
who pick fights over distorted pretexts.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.970
Nice one, Big Brother. 
That calls for applause.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:20.060
By the time we get back, you 
better have it cleaned up.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.040
Better have it cleaned up.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.540
This is the problem with 
the Shimogamo family.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.750
It really, really is.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.970
A "terrible nuisance."

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:33.640
Well, I guess this is 
just part of my training.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.410
Big Brother?

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.260
Yasaburo!

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.220
Can't see a thing.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.160
Meh.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.700
I'm gonna eat dinner here. It's gyudon.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.210
Gyudon, must be tasty.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:10.990
It's a real tragedy you got so used to 
that form that you can't change back.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.590
Have you been practicing at all?

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:18.560
The night I realized no matter what 
it wouldn't work I felt kinda down,

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.020
but I've given up now.

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:25.760
Plus, I never had any intention of going 
back to being a tanuki in the first place.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:28.240
You get what you wish for, yo.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:30.140
Do you still get lots of visitors?

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:33.180
Well it's calmed down a bit 
since last year, but...

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:39.350
You know, back when I was a tanuki 
even the pups called me stupid,

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:43.340
but now, so many people come to see me that 
I'd actually like some time to myself.

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.560
There's no time to feel lonely.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:49.270
You think you can bury me 
alive with all your worries?

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:56.180
Anyone feels ridiculous talkin' 
at a hole in the ground,

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:01.050
but that said, if there's no one to hear 
your worries then there's no point.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:06.090
That's where I come in, a forgotten no-good 
tanuki half dropped-out of society.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:09.030
There's no changing back for me.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:11.850
Anytime you come, you know I'm 
in the bottom of the well.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.950
The convenience factor is what made me a hit.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:19.410
Do you, like, give advice or something?

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:23.370
Well, I don't actually 
care about all those guys.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:29.850
And maybe there are benefits to having 
a listener you're not close to.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:35.640
At any rate, I'm a frog in a well. 
I "know nothing of the sea."

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:38.970
You don't care about Mother 
and the rest of us either?

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:42.970
Hey now, I'm not as rotten as all that.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:46.990
But you know, I'm a frog.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:50.310
Oh, now that you mention it, 
Yaichiro came by the other day.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.970
He did? What for?

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:57.660
He must have been worried about something. 
Left without saying a word, though.

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.570
You don't think he meant to 
lecture you and then gave up?

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.040
Didn't seem that way.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.660
He's got a lotta things to 
worry about, too, you know!

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.400
Yeah, I know.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:14.550
Lately I've been feelin' so sorry for him.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:21.170
He's doin' all he can to follow in our great 
father Shimogamo Soichiro's footsteps

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:25.070
but his little brothers are 
a frog, an idiot, and a kid.

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:26.770
Utterly useless.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.810
I can't argue with that. Wouldn't even try.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.670
Hey, Yasaburo.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:37.530
You were Father's favorite.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:42.930
I heard he even asked Prof. Akadama 
to pay special attention to you.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:46.250
"He's the one who's most like me."

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.670
That's the first I've heard of it.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.700
Do you remember the last 
thing Father said to you?

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:54.970
Nope.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:59.230
I can't remember Father's last 
words for the life of me.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.130
I'm mad at myself about that even now.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.150
Hey, where's Mother?

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:09.230
At that pool hall she goes to. Why'd you ask?

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:14.280
There's a big one comin'. I can't sit still.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.110
Raijin, God of Thunder, has arrived.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:27.280
I gotta pick up Yashiro.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.790
Yashiro...

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:41.550
<b>Renewed attack</b>

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:50.650
Say hello to... Shimogamo Yasaburo!

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:52.080
Big Brother!

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.180
Oh ho, Yasaburo is here.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:56.690
Bam!

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.690
<b>Higuchi Ichiyo</b>

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.950
<b>Electric Brandy factory</b>

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.950
<b>Ebisugawa power plant</b>

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:11.800
Yasaburo,

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:16.590
that little brother of yours left 
his work and fled the factory.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:21.110
It's not like that! Mother doesn't 
do well with thunder, so--

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:25.010
We're doing you a favor letting you work 
because you said you wanted to train!

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.160
And all you've been doing is causing trouble.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:30.560
We can't just stand by while 
you leave your work unfinished.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.810
That's exactly right, Big 
Brother. We can't stand by.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:38.440
A grown up is a grown up precisely because 
they do the work assigned to them--

00:12:38.630 --> 00:12:39.320
Go to hell!

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:41.620
...without complaining.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.320
I don't mean to stick my 
nose in your business--

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:45.790
Go to hell!

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:51.850
but I'm concerned about the 
future of the Shimogamo family!

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:55.520
The Shimogamo family is a bunch 
of blockheads, Big Brother.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:59.290
The second eldest is a frog, 
the third is an idiot,

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:02.510
and this is about all we can 
expect of the youngest brother.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:05.380
We Ebisugawas have to step it up.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:08.030
Ah, the future of tanuki 
society is looking bleak.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:10.220
We'll be okay as long as 
you're here, Big Brother!

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:13.230
You're one of those "stars of hope."

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.660
Ginkaku,

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:18.930
"Higuchi Ichiyo" is a person's 
name, not fancy vocab.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:26.030
<b>Higuchi Ichiyo</b>

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:23.510
You can't trick me! Are 
you a vocabulary teacher?

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.030
Big Brother, is it really a name?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.550
No, no, no, don't believe a word of that.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:30.600
"Higuchi Ichiyo" means

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:35.770
"a solitary dead leaf is stuck 
on the end of the drain spout."

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:39.060
It's enlightened vocabulary that 
expresses the melancholy of autumn.

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:41.370
I read it in a book!

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:45.470
Right! I pretty much knew that.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:49.380
Now then, hand over your puny little brother.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:51.890
We'll teach him a lesson.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:56.110
Father gave us carte blanche.

00:13:56.110 --> 00:14:00.180
Our job is to teach him the 
discipline having a job entails.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:04.400
And we won't leave our work unfinished!

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.520
So let's have that little brother of yours...

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.090
I don't think so!

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.540
You're being selfish as usual, huh.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:18.540
I am forever lamenting guys like you who
 make light of tanuki society rules.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:23.420
I'm forever thinking that you guys are 
unqualified to say stuff like that to us.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:26.670
Oh, we <i>are</i> qualified. Because we're great.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.550
Big Brother, Mother's in trouble.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.780
I know.

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:35.890
We'll retreat now and come back later with a 
perfectly dirty scheme to really shut them up.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:37.890
Kinkaku, Ginkaku!

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.210
Yaichiro!

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:52.750
Ahh, my butt!

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:58.300
Oh boy, now I'm flying. Somebody catch me...

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:03.700
KamoTiger, you jerk!

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:06.460
I mean, Shimogamo Yaichiro.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:30.920
Not there!

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:34.040
I have a whole lot of problems 
with you biting me there!

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:59.720
Why are you dilly-dallying?! 
Hurry up and get on!

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:06.820
Why don't you fight back when those 
Ebisugawa guys insult you like that?

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:10.920
You don't have the backbone to risk yourself
 in order to protect your family's honor?!

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:15.270
I dunno what you mean by our 
"family's honor" or whatever.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:20.120
A guy who thinks everything's fine 
as long as he's having fun wouldn't!

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:23.190
I swear, you are the most unfilial brat!

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:26.450
Father is surely suffering in the next world.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:30.250
Father wasn't the type of tanuki 
who cared about stuff like that.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:34.100
And Big Brother, I told them to go to hell!

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.180
Is the Prince in black here?

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:46.440
As soon as it started thundering he 
seemed kind of in a hurry, but...

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:49.520
in all the hubbub over the tanuki, 
I'm not sure where he went.

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.030
Hubbub over a tanuki?

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.190
Supposedly a tanuki showed up in that cafe.

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:55.330
And what happened to that tanuki?

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:57.880
At some point it went off somewhere.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:16:59.950
Thanks.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:07.420
Mother, you just had to 
go play pool, didn't you!

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:11.770
We must send a messenger immediately 
to call all the tanuki of Kyoto

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:14.380
and carry out an emergency search!

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:17.220
You make such a fuss over everything.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:20.180
But what'll we do if she 
gets hit by a car again?!

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:25.650
You really think she's gonna run on purpose 
to Gojo or Shijo where there's a ton of cars?

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:28.480
Anyways, let's split up and 
search around the bridge.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:32.580
Right, let's take care of that first. 
I'll take command!

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:35.630
First, Yaichiro will head 
for Doshisha University!

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:39.310
Ah, wait I'm Yaichiro. 
I'll look around Doshisha University!

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:43.040
Yasaburo, go north of the Kamogawa river!
 Yashiro, head across the bridge!

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:46.120
South of the Kamogawa, Yasaburo! 
You'll search there!

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:48.780
I can't go north and south at the same time.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:50.000
Okay, then Yajiro!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:53.710
Yajiro is in a well. On 
top of that, he's a frog.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:57.530
How useless does he have 
to be before he is happy?!

00:17:57.530 --> 00:17:59.060
What have I done to deserve this?

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:03.020
Why are little brothers 
all such useless guys?

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:06.730
Please calm down. I'm most 
worried about you at this point.

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.280
Let's just split up and look.

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:22.030
Is she there?

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.230
No.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.580
I wonder where she went.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.310
Mother!

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:46.650
Phew!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.270
Crud!

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.430
You were under the bridge the whole time?

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:57.770
The daughter of the 
Ebisugawas stayed with me.

00:18:57.770 --> 00:19:01.960
Just as I was about to fall 
in the river, she saved me.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:04.500
Mother, this way!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.290
Kaisei?

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:17.430
How long are you gonna stand 
around? Hurry up and go home!

00:19:17.430 --> 00:19:19.420
Well I should thank you.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.360
Forget about it.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:25.280
Are you trying to give 
your mother a cold? Idiot!

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:26.820
Thanks.

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:31.190
Give my regards to your shithead 
brothers Kinkaku and Ginkaku,

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.790
although I don't think 
they'll be back for a while.

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:36.290
Get home safely.

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:40.490
What were you doing?

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.110
I said thanks.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:45.920
The Ebisugawas can all go to hell,

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:47.990
but she's different.

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:01.010
I'm glad I have you guys.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:06.020
Even if Soichiro isn't 
here, I still have you.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:13.890
Our dad was one of the well-known, 
great tanuki of Kyoto.

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:19.110
He was respected by many tanuki and with 
that influence, he united tanuki society,

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:23.500
but regrettably, several 
years ago he passed away.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:27.240
He was eaten, as an ingredient in a hot pot.

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:30.500
When we found out that dad had died,

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:34.260
we brothers were dumbfounded for half a day

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:36.550
and then finally started to cry.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:41.520
As long as tanuki exist there will be 
times they are boiled to make hot pot.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:43.920
So what's so unusual about it?

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:47.650
Grow up to be splendid 
tanuki like your father,

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:50.650
who can turn up your noses at 
the Friday Fellows' hot pot!

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:54.470
Just don't end up getting 
boiled in one like him!

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:58.680
Please, anyone but you. 
Never get boiled in a hot pot!

00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:13.810
Mother, you raised splendid 
kids just like you said,

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.340
except us three are useless.

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:19.190
And on top of that, one is a frog.

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:22.770
I don't care if you're 
a frog or what you are.

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:26.580
I'm just happy to have you all in this world.

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:30.560
Plus, you're all great tanuki.

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:33.600
I know it.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:39.000
Our mother doesn't believe 
for one minute that

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:43.530
her children are notorious 
losers in tanuki society.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:46.220
She has no doubt that

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:51.750
every last one of us kids are fit to follow 
in the footsteps of our deceased dad.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.870
Our dad was great,

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:59.490
and you know, so is our mom.

00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:33.390
Benten did what?!

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:36.100
Of all the shameless, outrageous--

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:39.960
You can't watch! Nobody can see this but me!

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Yakushibo's Inner Parlor</b>
